{
  "scope": "Focused offline macOS CardPointers 8.1.4 Apple integration path; no runtime execution",
  "findings": {
    "CPAI-01": {
      "observations": [
        "Info.plist separates the macOS WidgetKit extension from the Intents service, with PointersWidgetOneIntent and an explicit IntentHandler principal class in the latter.",
        "Both signed extension entitlement records contain the same App Group identifiers."
      ],
      "inference": [
        "The selected options provider is an Intents configuration path with shared persistence capability."
      ],
      "limits": [
        "Entitlements and declarations do not prove WidgetKit timeline entry routing or successful runtime data access."
      ]
    },
    "CPAI-02": {
      "observations": [
        "The named Objective-C provideSelectedPointerOptionsCollectionForPointersWidgetOne:withCompletion: method copies the completion block and branches to the selected Swift body.",
        "That body loads PersistenceController.shared, obtains its container field at +0x10, calls viewContext, and passes sortBy 3 to getDefaultDBPointerParents.",
        "Shared initialization leads to storeURL(for:databaseName:) with group.getcardpointers.app and cardpointers; storeURL appends .sqlite.",
        "The constructor uses NSPersistentContainer and reaches loadPersistentStoresWithCompletionHandler; this is an initialization boundary, not proof that the extension makes no writes."
      ],
      "inference": [
        "The options provider reads its candidate parents through the shared App Group Core Data setup."
      ],
      "limits": [
        "No actual store directory or user database was opened. Store migration/retry and completion error handling were not expanded."
      ]
    },
    "CPAI-03": {
      "observations": [
        "The getDefaultDBPointerParents wrapper supplies closure 0x1001b5368 to the performAndWait wrapper; the closure calls fetch body 0x1001b3f08.",
        "The fetch entity is DBPointerParent, with predicate is_favorite == YES OR lastViewedAt != nil OR entity == %@.",
        "For sortBy 3, it takes the default sort branch, using ascending sort_order then ascending name.",
        "A thrown fetch error is released and replaced by the canonical empty array."
      ],
      "inference": [
        "Candidate order is local Core Data order for this configuration list."
      ],
      "limits": [
        "The OR entity predicate must not be summarized as favorites-only. No recommendation ranking or current data population is established."
      ]
    },
    "CPAI-04": {
      "observations": [
        "Each fetched parent is mapped to WidgetOnePointer using its id converted to a String, smartTitle, optional display image, and nil subtitle.",
        "The mapper tries Data(contentsOf:) for its image URL and uses INImage.imageWithURL on the observed error branch.",
        "The body always creates the fallback option and inserts it via a range 0,0 array helper before constructing INObjectCollection.",
        "The fallback factory uses identifier String(0), Last Viewed, and Show the last pointer viewed in the app.",
        "The completion block is invoked with the collection and a nil error argument."
      ],
      "inference": [
        "A fetch failure can still produce the fixed Last Viewed configuration choice; the range arguments indicate insertion at the start."
      ],
      "limits": [
        "The actual selected-pointer resolver and rendered widget last-viewed lookup were not traced. Image URL derivation and actual file/network availability are not established. Missing App Group container is fatalError, not a graceful storage fallback."
      ]
    },
    "CPAI-05": {
      "observations": [
        "CPWidgetExtension contains its own named options method and a 616-byte body; exact calls resolve to the same named PersistenceController.shared and getDefaultDBPointerParents helpers.",
        "The two body hashes differ, so this is a selected call-level comparison rather than byte equivalence."
      ],
      "inference": [
        "The WidgetKit executable also ships this configuration helper implementation."
      ],
      "limits": [
        "No call from a WidgetKit timeline/provider entry to this helper was recovered. Timeline creation, placeholder/snapshot choice, reload policy, refresh cadence, on-device rendering, and iPad equivalence remain open."
      ]
    }
  },
